What is the purpose of the <meta> tag?
Answer:
It provides metadata about the HTML document, such as:
• Character encoding (<meta charset="UTF-8">)
• Viewport settings (<meta name="viewport" content="width=devicewidth, initial-scale=1.0">)
• SEO descriptions (<meta name="description" content="...">)

Meta tags are placed inside the <head> section of an HTML page and provide information about the webpage to search engines and browsers.
The <meta> tag lives in the <head> and gives extra info about your web page, like what character set it uses, a description for search engines, or settings for mobile screens. It’s not visible to users but helps browsers and Google understand your page better.

Are Meta Tags Important for SEO?
👉 YES — but in two ways:
Direct impact (ranking factors)
Indirect impact (CTR, user behavior)
<meta name="description" content="Learn frontend easily">

Meta tags do NOT appear on the visible webpage UI.
They are placed inside the <head> section of an HTML document and are used by:
Browsers
Search engines
