What is the difference between defer and async in <script>?

Async:  Script loads in parallel and executes immediately when ready
HTML parsing continues
Script downloads in background
Executes as soon as downloaded
Order NOT guaranteed

defer (Deferred Execution): Script loads in parallel but executes after HTML is fully parsed
HTML parsing continues
Script downloads in background
Executes after DOM is ready
Order is maintained
