What is the purpose of the <template> tag?

The <template> tag is used to store HTML content that is not rendered immediately, but can be used later using JavaScript.
It holds HTML content that can be cloned and inserted via JavaScript (not rendered by default)

<template id="card">
  <div class="box">
    <h2>Title</h2>
  </div>
</template>
This will NOT appear on the page

Using It with JavaScript
<script>
  let temp = document.getElementById("card");
  let clone = temp.content.cloneNode(true);
  document.body.appendChild(clone);
</script>
